CHARACTER=A cheerful young red panda explorer: rusty red-orange fur, a white face mask with white cheeks and a white muzzle, two white eyebrow spots above the eyes, rounded rust ears with white edges, and a dark-brown nose. Dark-brown mitten paws. A big bushy tail with clear alternating rings of rust red and cream: it comes out from behind the hips on the right side of the picture, sweeps out sideways and curves upward in one clean soft shape, its tip ending at about belt height, fully visible beside the body, below the hand and clear of it, with plain background between the tail and the leg and between the tail and the arm. A mustard-yellow long-sleeved field jacket with two flapped chest pockets and plain cuffs, olive-green trousers held by a brown belt, and brown lace-up hiking boots. Both paws are empty: no tools or props.
PIECES=Row 1: head base (the furry rust red panda head with its white face mask: white cheeks, white muzzle, the two white eyebrow spots and the dark-brown nose, plain fur eye areas), left ear, right ear (rounded rust ears with white edges). Row 2: torso (the mustard-yellow field jacket with its collar, its button placket and its two flapped chest pockets, continuing up into a short rust fur neck and ending at the bottom hem of the jacket just above the belt; both shoulders are rounded jacket, and the jacket sides are painted down to the hem; no sleeves, belt or trousers on it), hips (only the top of the olive-green trousers: the brown belt with its buckle and the trousers below it down to the crotch and no further, painted whole, with two rounded leg openings just below the crotch; no trouser legs on it). Row 3: four separate sleeve pieces, each painted upright: left upper arm, right upper arm (the upper half of the mustard-yellow sleeve only, from shoulder to elbow, rounded at both ends, no cuff), left forearm, right forearm (the lower half of the mustard-yellow sleeve only, from elbow to wrist, rounded at the top, with its cuff at the bottom); then left paw, right paw (dark-brown mitten paws, open and relaxed, rounded at the wrist). Row 4: left leg, right leg (one olive-green trouser leg each, from the crotch down to its hem, exactly as long and as wide as in image_1, rounded at the top, with nothing below the hem), left boot, right boot (brown lace-up hiking boots, rounded at the top), tail (the big bushy tail with its alternating rust and cream rings exactly as image_1 holds it: its narrow rounded root at the lower left, where it joins behind the trousers, the tail sweeping right along the bottom and curving up into a tall J with its rounded rust tip at the top).
HANDS=relaxed (exactly the paw of image_1, open and relaxed); open (palm facing the viewer, all fingers spread wide, as in a wave); fist (palm side facing the viewer: the fingers curled into a soft round fist, the curled fingers and the thumb across them visible); point (the palm facing the viewer: index finger stretched straight down, the other fingers curled onto the palm); thumbs-up (fingers curled into a fist, thumb sticking straight out sideways, away from the body); grip (fingers curled loosely forward and the thumb pressed against the side of the first finger, as when pinching something thin).
POSES=Row 1: left boot, left boot on tiptoe, right boot, right boot on tiptoe (brown lace-up hiking boots; on tiptoe the boot is seen from the front with its toe pointing down and its sole tilted towards the viewer, as when jumping, with its rounded ankle end still at the top). Row 2: tail (the big bushy tail exactly as it is in image_1, at the same size, with the same alternating rust and cream rings: its narrow rounded root at the lower left, where it joins behind the trousers, the tail sweeping right along the bottom and curving up into a tall J, its rounded rust tip at the top; one clean soft shape).
SLEEVE=mustard-yellow field-jacket sleeve with its turned-back cuff and small cuff button
PROPS=Left: a small white flag on a thin straight wooden stick: the stick is vertical, as long as the character's whole arm, and the plain white rectangular cloth hangs from the top third of the stick out to the right with two soft folds; nothing is drawn on the cloth. Right: a low wooden hurdle seen straight from the front: two short upright posts on small feet and one horizontal crossbar painted red and white, about as tall as the character's boots and trousers up to the knee, and about as wide as the character's hips.
POINT=point, the palm facing the viewer: index finger stretched straight down, the other fingers curled onto the palm with their rounded fingertips showing, wrist up, chunky dark-brown mitten paw like image_1.
POINT2=point, seen from the palm side: a slightly lighter brown palm pad fills the middle of the hand, the short thumb lies folded across the front of the palm, the middle, ring and little fingers are curled up onto the palm with their rounded fingertips facing the viewer, and only the index finger is stretched straight down; wrist up, a chunky dark-brown mitten paw like image_1.
